values
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG01', 1, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 0,
   'CG01 • Enrollment and Commercial Logbook Audit',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Existing 250 total/100 powered/50 airplane/100 PIC/50 airplane PIC/50 XC PIC/10 airplane XC PIC, category/class and prior training evidence. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG02', 1, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 1,
   'CG02 • Commercial Privileges and Operations',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. §61.133, §119.1(e), common carriage/holding out, compensation, operational control and business cases. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG03', 1, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 2,
   'CG03 • Commercial Aerodynamics and Performance',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Energy, accelerated stalls, maneuver theory, altitude/density and realistic margins. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG04', 1, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 3,
   'CG04 • Aircraft Systems and Equipment Qualifications',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Actual aircraft limitations, performance, avionics; separate complex/TAA/turbine evaluation under §61.129(j). Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG05', 1, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 4,
   'CG05 • Advanced Maneuvers Briefing',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Chandelles, lazy eights, steep spirals, eights on pylons and commercial tolerances. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C01', 1, 'Dual', 1.5, 0.5, 2.0, 5,
   'C01 • Enrollment, Commercial Experience Audit and Baseline',
   'Dual, 1.5 aircraft hrs. Audit certificates, prior total/PIC/XC/instrument experience, select target aircraft and assess prior proficiency. Completion: accurate experience-gap plan; identify applicable commercial privileges and operating limits. Recording: date, actual aircraft duration, PIC/dual/solo or performing-PIC mode, applicable maneuver/ACS task rating, instructor, logbook reference, and any required route/night/advanced-aircraft evidence; advanced training requires equipment qualification documentation.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C02', 1, 'Dual', 1.5, 0.5, 2.0, 6,
   'C02 • Commercial Airwork and Coordination',
   'Dual, 1.5 aircraft hrs. Power/trim combinations, slow flight, energy management and maneuver setup. Completion: consistent control, situational awareness, configuration and clearance management.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C03', 1, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 7,
   'C03 • Steep Turns and Steep Spirals',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Commercial steep turns, steep spirals and energy control. Completion: consistent ACS-level maneuver accuracy and wind/traffic awareness.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C04', 1, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 8,
   'C04 • Chandelles Introduction',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Maximum-performance climbing turn, coordination, pitch/power sequencing, clearing. Completion: appropriate entry and recovery with ACS-aligned criteria.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C05', 1, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 9,
   'C05 • Lazy Eights Introduction',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Changing pitch, bank and airspeed throughout paired 180-degree turns. Completion: smooth coordinated energy management without excessive prompting.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C06', 1, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 10,
   'C06 • Eights on Pylons',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Pivotal altitude, wind effects, reference selection and safe escape. Completion: maintain a suitable pivotal relationship and safe ground clearance.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C07', 1, 'Dual evaluation', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 11,
   'C07 • Stage Check 1 — Performance Fundamentals',
   'Dual evaluation, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Evaluate steep turns, chandelles, lazy eights, eights on pylons, aircraft control and risk management. Completion: meets stage standard; unresolved deficiencies trigger remediation. Stage 1 gate: instructor verifies demonstrated stage proficiency, unresolved safety-critical deficits, legally qualifying training/experience documentation and readiness for the next activity. Stage checks do not grant pilot privileges or certify §61.129 completion.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG06', 2, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 12,
   'CG06 • Commercial Landings and Emergencies',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Power-off 180, short/soft fields, engine failure, airport contingencies and decision-making. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C08', 2, 'Dual', 1.5, 0.5, 2.0, 13,
   'C08 • Commercial Normal and Crosswind Operations',
   'Dual, 1.5 aircraft hrs. Professional preflight, passenger management, airport operations, normal/crosswind takeoffs and landings. Completion: safe, precise, independent operational workflow.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C09', 2, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 14,
   'C09 • Short-Field and Soft-Field Proficiency',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Short-field and soft-field takeoffs/landings, performance margins, abort decisions. Completion: applicable ACS tolerances and aircraft-limit compliance.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C10', 2, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 15,
   'C10 • Power-Off 180° Accuracy Landing I',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Energy planning, configuration sequencing, touchdown accuracy and go-around decision. Completion: reliable energy management; no forced unsafe touchdown.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C11', 2, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 16,
   'C11 • Power-Off 180° Accuracy Landing II',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Repeat accuracy approaches with wind, weight, and traffic variations. Completion: meets ACS standards without instructor technique prompts.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C12', 2, 'Dual', 1.5, 0.5, 2.0, 17,
   'C12 • Accelerated Stalls and Stall Risk',
   'Dual, 1.5 aircraft hrs. Accelerated stalls where applicable, stall/spin avoidance and coordinated recovery. Completion: prompt first-indication recognition and correct recovery.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C13', 2, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 18,
   'C13 • Emergency Operations and System Failures',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Emergency descent, simulated power loss, system malfunctions, forced landing and postflight judgment. Completion: prioritize aircraft control, select reachable landing options, use checklists correctly.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C14', 2, 'Dual evaluation', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 19,
   'C14 • Stage Check 2 — Commercial Maneuver Proficiency',
   'Dual evaluation, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Integrated maneuvers, landings, emergencies, systems and judgment. Completion: demonstrates independent stage-level commercial proficiency. Stage 2 gate: instructor verifies demonstrated stage proficiency, unresolved safety-critical deficits, legally qualifying training/experience documentation and readiness for the next activity. Stage checks do not grant pilot privileges or certify §61.129 completion.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG07', 3, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 20,
   'CG07 • Advanced-Aircraft Systems and Automation',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Equipment-dependent training, malfunction scenarios and documentation. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG08', 3, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 21,
   'CG08 • Day/Night XC and 300-NM Route Workshop',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Commercial-specific >100 NM dual day/night routes, >=300 NM solo/performing-PIC routes with one >=250 NM straight-line landing. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG09', 3, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 22,
   'CG09 • Night VFR Tower and PIC-Duty Planning',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Tower status, 10 takeoffs/landings, 5 night hours, duty mode and flight authorization. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG10', 3, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 23,
   'CG10 • Instrument-Training Evidence Audit',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Evaluate prior instrument-rating instruction evidence by specific §61.129 maneuver; plan any deficiencies. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C15', 3, 'Dual XC', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 24,
   'C15 • Day Dual Commercial Cross-Country',
   'Dual XC, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Qualifying single-engine daytime training flight more than 100 NM straight-line from original point of departure, at least 2 hours. Completion: confirm actual route, departure and arrival, instructor status, and §61.129(a)(3)(iii) eligibility.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C16', 3, 'Dual XC night', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 25,
   'C16 • Night Dual Commercial Cross-Country',
   'Dual XC night, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Qualifying single-engine nighttime training flight more than 100 NM straight-line from original point of departure, at least 2 hours. Completion: confirm nighttime conditions, route, instructor and §61.129(a)(3)(iv).'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C17', 3, 'Dual instrument', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 26,
   'C17 • Instrument Training Audit and Refresher',
   'Dual instrument, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Airplane view-limited instrument tasks: attitude, partial-panel, unusual attitudes, intercept/track; evaluate prior evidence. Completion: log qualifying instructor instrument training distinctly, reconcile 10 total/5 single-engine airplane requirements; add training as necessary.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C18', 3, 'Dual qualifying aircraft', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 27,
   'C18 • Complex/TAA/Turbine Orientation I',
   'Dual qualifying aircraft, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Systems/limitations, advanced automation or retractable gear/constant speed prop as applicable, workload management. Completion: verify aircraft actually meets §61.129(a)(3)(ii)/(j), and train within aircraft limitations.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C19', 3, 'Dual qualifying aircraft', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 28,
   'C19 • Complex/TAA/Turbine Operations II',
   'Dual qualifying aircraft, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Advanced-aircraft departures/arrivals, failures, abnormal procedures, checklist discipline. Completion: safe independent systems management at lesson standard.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C20', 3, 'Dual qualifying aircraft', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 29,
   'C20 • Complex/TAA/Turbine Operations III',
   'Dual qualifying aircraft, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Advanced maneuvers, navigation, diversion and scenario work. Completion: demonstrate appropriate proficiency; record qualifying dual instruction.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C21', 3, 'Dual qualifying aircraft', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 30,
   'C21 • Complex/TAA/Turbine Operations IV',
   'Dual qualifying aircraft, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Complete qualifying advanced-aircraft training and check the 10-hour requirement. Completion: at least 10 actual qualifying hours only with appropriate aircraft and logged authorized instruction.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C22', 3, 'Solo or performing PIC', 5.5, 0.5, 6.0, 31,
   'C22 • 300-NM Solo / Performing-PIC Cross-Country',
   'Solo or performing PIC, 5.5 aircraft hrs. One flight >=300 NM total distance, landings at >=3 points, one landing >=250 NM straight line from original departure; §61.129(a)(4)(i). Completion: actual route/distance, 3 points, PIC-duty mode, instructor presence/limitations and logbook verified.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C23', 3, 'Solo or performing PIC', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 32,
   'C23 • Night VFR Solo / Performing-PIC I',
   'Solo or performing PIC, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Night VFR, towered airport operations; 10 full-stop landings and 10 takeoffs with traffic-pattern flights required across night lessons. Completion: count actual night VFR and tower operating status; verify authorized PIC-duty mode.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C24', 3, 'Solo or performing PIC', 2.5, 0.5, 3.0, 33,
   'C24 • Night VFR Solo / Performing-PIC II',
   'Solo or performing PIC, 2.5 aircraft hrs. Complete >=5 qualifying night VFR hours and required 10 takeoffs/landings at operating tower. Completion: instructor verifies the precise §61.129(a)(4)(ii) record.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C25', 3, 'Solo or performing PIC', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 34,
   'C25 • Independent PIC-Duty Consolidation / Experience Audit',
   'Solo or performing PIC, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Complete remaining 10-hour solo/performance-of-PIC-duties category, flight planning, ADM and logged deficiencies. Completion: do not double count nonqualifying dual instruction or conflate safety-pilot time with required duties.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C26', 3, 'Dual evaluation', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 35,
   'C26 • Stage Check 3 — Experience and Advanced Proficiency',
   'Dual evaluation, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Review actual §61.129 experience and advanced maneuvers, systems, emergency and professional decisions. Completion: clear qualification gaps and identify requirements still outstanding; stage check itself not certification. Stage 3 gate: instructor verifies demonstrated stage proficiency, unresolved safety-critical deficits, legally qualifying training/experience documentation and readiness for the next activity. Stage checks do not grant pilot privileges or certify §61.129 completion.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG11', 4, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 36,
   'CG11 • Commercial Regulations/ACS Oral Workshop',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Risk management, airspace, weather, flight planning, §61.127 and ACS knowledge. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'CG12', 4, 'Ground', 0.0, 1.5, 1.5, 37,
   'CG12 • Final Experience, Endorsements and Mock Oral',
   'Ground, 1.5 hrs. Training records, recency, privileges/limitations, IACRA/test records and sign-off. Completion: student demonstrates scenario-based understanding, references controlling regulations and aircraft sources, and corrects deficiencies before applicable stage progression.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C27', 4, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 38,
   'C27 • Integrated Commercial ACS Scenario Flight',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Business/compensation scenario, flight planning, maneuvers, commercial landings, emergencies. Completion: all assigned applicable ACS tasks satisfactorily demonstrated.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C28', 4, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 39,
   'C28 • Performance and Landing Precision Review',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Focus on chandelles, lazy eights, eights on pylons, steep spirals and power-off 180. Completion: ACS tolerances, judgment and stable landing outcomes.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C29', 4, 'Dual evaluation', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 40,
   'C29 • Mock Commercial Practical Test / Oral',
   'Dual evaluation, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Scenario oral on §119/61/91 privileges/limitations, aeronautical knowledge, aircraft and ACS flight tasks. Completion: record satisfactory/deficient ACS evidence; assign correction plan.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C30', 4, 'Dual', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 41,
   'C30 • Targeted Correction and Recent Preparation',
   'Dual, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Recheck weak ACS tasks, instrument/time-building gaps if any, recent practical test prep. Completion: qualifying 3 hours in preceding two calendar months, plus ACS performance.'),
  ('72c2d8cd-02e6-493b-83ce-7b7d190cd2b6', 'C31', 4, 'Dual evaluation', 2.0, 0.5, 2.5, 42,
   'C31 • Final Stage Check and Certification Readiness',
   'Dual evaluation, 2.0 aircraft hrs. Full eligibility/aeronautical-experience, knowledge test, endorsements, application, aircraft and ACS record review. Completion: independent authorized instructor recommendation; release only if all applicable requirements met. Stage 4 gate: instructor verifies demonstrated stage proficiency, unresolved safety-critical deficits, legally qualifying training/experience documentation and readiness for the next activity. Stage checks do not grant pilot privileges or certify §61.129 completion.');

